  "distinctions": [
    "Botanical motifs retain their depicted morphology: a split monstera leaf, a fan-shaped ginkgo leaf, a cacao pod with seeds and a maize cob with rows of kernels are substantive visual differences, not colour or fabric variants.",
    "Geometric prints are grouped when their primary layout is equivalent; shifted rectilinear elements, broken polygon borders, open arcs and assembled spirals are explicitly consolidated.",
    "Different represented functions remain distinct: a turning cylindrical bag closure and a sliding bar closure use different operations; a single slit sleeve and a ladder of connecting cuff strips have different physical constructions.",
    "Composite scenes are treated as a coherent scenario: a courtyard fountain or a train crossing a bridge is not fragmented into labels for every incidental object."
  ],
